-- title:
--   Base change of the L₀-generated extra level at ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$, a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, natural numbers $N$, $m$, $\ell$, a further $\mathbb Z$-submodule $L_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, commutative rings $S,S'$ and a ring homomorphism $\varphi : S \to S'$ such that the image of $\ell$ in $S$ is a unit. Let $u=(E,\mathcal P)$ be a fake elliptic curve for $(\Lambda,N)$ over $S$ with a full level-$m$ structure, $u'=(E',\mathcal P')$ one over $S'$, and assume `FakeEllipticCurve.WithFullLevel.IsPullback` holds for $\varphi$: there are a morphism $g : E'.A \to E.A$ making $E'.A$ the fibre product of $E.A$ and $\operatorname{Spec} S'$ over $\operatorname{Spec} S$, such that $g$ carries the relative group law of $E'$ to that of $E$ on points, commutes with the $\Lambda$-actions ($E'.\mathrm{act}\,x$ followed by $g$ equals $g$ followed by $E.\mathrm{act}\,x$), carries any $T$-point factoring through $E'.\mathrm{lev}$ to one factoring through $E.\mathrm{lev}$, and satisfies $\mathcal P'$ followed by $g$ $=$ $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $\mathcal P$. Let $K$ be an extra level at $\ell$ on $E$ and $K'$ one on $E'$, and assume their geometric points are cut out by $L_0$: for every algebraically closed field $k$, every $sk : S \to k$ and every $k$-point $Q$ of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(sk)$, $Q$ factors through $K.\mathrm{levK}$ if and only if $Q = \mathrm{act}(x)$ applied to the $\lfloor m/\ell\rfloor$-fold sum of the point obtained from $\mathcal P$ at $(k,sk)$ for some $x \in \Lambda$ lying in $L_0$, and the analogous description with $E'$, $K'$, $\mathcal P'$ and maps $S' \to k$. The conclusion is `FakeEllipticCurve.WithExtraLevel.IsPullback` for $\varphi$ and the pairs $(E,K)$, $(E',K')$: a cartesian $g$ compatible with the group laws and the $\Lambda$-actions as above such that, for every $T$-point $P$ of $E'$ over $S'$, a factorisation of $P$ through $E'.\mathrm{lev}$ yields a factorisation of $P$ followed by $g$ through $E.\mathrm{lev}$, and a factorisation of $P$ through $K'.\mathrm{levK}$ yields a factorisation of $P$ followed by $g$ through $K.\mathrm{levK}$. Note that the extra-level clause is the one-directional transport of factorisations, not an isomorphism $K' \cong K \times_{\operatorname{Spec} S} \operatorname{Spec} S'$, and that $m/\ell$ is natural-number division.
--
--   This is the base-change compatibility of the auxiliary level structure at $\ell$ generated by a submodule $L_0$ acting on the $\lfloor m/\ell\rfloor$-multiple of the full level-$m$ point: it says that the cartesian square of fake elliptic curves with full level $m$ remains a cartesian square once both sides are equipped with their $L_0$-generated extra levels. It is used in the verification that the fine moduli problem produces algebraic families with extra level matching the analytic lattice data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_QM_FakeEllipticCurve_WithFullLevel_withExtraLevel_isPullback_of_isPullback_of_forall_factorsThrough_iff.lean

